<GuidePageLayout title="Connect ChatGPT" description="Add Tuwa to ChatGPT as a connector: turn it on in Tuwa, add the URL in ChatGPT, sign in, and disconnect at any time." locale="en" path="/guide/chatgpt/">
<p>With the connector, ChatGPT can read your Tuwa readings, sessions and plan, show the day's card in the chat, and send you a plan draft to review. Tuwa still makes the day's go, modify or hold decision in the app. The connector is free and off until you turn it on.</p>

<p>The ChatGPT pictures on this page are drawings, not screenshots. ChatGPT can change its screens, so follow the words in bold.</p>

<h2>What you need</h2>
<ul>
<li>A Tuwa account and Tuwa 1.7.6 or later on your iPhone.</li>
<li>ChatGPT on the web. OpenAI's help page says you cannot connect a custom MCP server on mobile.</li>
<li>A plan that allows it. OpenAI's help page names three cases:
<ul>
<li><strong>Pro:</strong> read and fetch permissions only, so ChatGPT may not be able to send you a plan draft.</li>
<li><strong>Business:</strong> only admins and owners can add a server.</li>
<li><strong>Enterprise and Edu:</strong> admins and owners, and members an admin permits.</li>
</ul>
That page does not name Free or Plus. If your account cannot add a server, use <a href="/guide/claude/">Claude</a> or the <strong>Copy the prompt</strong> route in the <a href="/guide/quick-start/">quick start</a>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>1. Turn it on in Tuwa</h2>
<ol>
<li>Open <strong>Profile</strong> › <strong>Legal</strong> › <strong>AI connector</strong>.</li>
<li>Read <strong>What is sent</strong>, <strong>Never sent</strong> and <strong>Kept</strong>.</li>
<li>Turn on <strong>Allow the AI connector</strong>. Until you do, Tuwa gives your AI app nothing.</li>
</ol>
<GuideShots caption="Profile › Legal › AI connector, in the Tuwa app (demo account)." shots={[{ src: shots.connector, alt: 'Tuwa AI connector screen: what is sent, what is never sent and what is kept' }]} />

<h2>2. Add Tuwa in ChatGPT</h2>
<ol>
<li>Open <code>chatgpt.com/plugins</code>. Select the plus button, then <strong>Add custom MCP server</strong>. You do not need to turn on Developer Mode first.</li>
</ol>
<GuideFigure caption="Plugins › + › Add custom MCP server."><ConnectPlates plate="chatgpt-path" /></GuideFigure>
<ol start="2">
<li>Name: <code>Tuwa</code>. Connection: <code>https://mcp.tuwa.app/mcp</code>. Authentication: <strong>OAuth</strong>.</li>
<li>ChatGPT shows a warning for each custom server. Read it and select <strong>I understand and want to continue</strong>.</li>
<li>Select <strong>Create as a plugin</strong>, check the tools it found, then install the plugin.</li>
</ol>
<GuideFigure caption="Type the URL exactly and choose OAuth."><ConnectPlates plate="chatgpt-form" /></GuideFigure>
<p>Tuwa is not in ChatGPT's plugin directory today, so add it by this URL.</p>

<h2>3. Sign in and allow</h2>
<p>A Tuwa page opens at tuwa.app. Sign in the way you sign in to the app — Apple, Google, or your email with your password or a one-time code — and choose <strong>Allow</strong>.</p>
<GuideFigure caption="Sign in on tuwa.app, then choose Allow."><ConnectPlates plate="signin" /><ConnectPlates plate="allow" client="ChatGPT" /></GuideFigure>

<h2>4. Ask ChatGPT</h2>
<p>Start a new chat. Type <code>@</code> in the prompt box, select Tuwa, and ask, for example: "Where am I in my plan?" Your choice applies to that message, so type <code>@</code> again when a later question needs new data.</p>
<GuideFigure caption="Type @, select Tuwa, then ask."><ConnectPlates plate="chatgpt-chat" /></GuideFigure>

<h2>What ChatGPT can read, and what it never gets</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>It can read:</strong> your recovery and sleep scores (composite scores only), the day's decision, your logged sessions and training load, your personal records, and your plan — its position and its text.</li>
<li><strong>It can send:</strong> a plan draft. The draft waits for you: a row <strong>A plan arrived from your AI · Review</strong> appears on Today and Log. Open it, check the plan, then tap <strong>Activate this plan</strong> or <strong>Dismiss this draft</strong>. Tuwa never activates a draft by itself.</li>
<li><strong>It cannot:</strong> change your plan, log a workout or answer your check-in.</li>
<li><strong>Never sent:</strong> no number from Apple Health — no heart rate, HRV, sleep time, temperature or cycle data.</li>
</ul>
<GuideFigure caption="A draft from your AI waits on Today and Log until you open it." kind="phones">
<DrawnPhone title="Today" options={[{ label: 'A plan arrived from your AI · Review', hot: true }]} />
<DrawnPhone title="From your AI" sub="Your AI sent this plan as a draft. Nothing changes until you activate it." options={[{ label: 'Activate this plan', hot: true }, { label: 'Dismiss this draft' }]} />
</GuideFigure>
<p>The full list of tools is on the <a href="/connector/">connector page</a>; what is kept is in the <a href="/privacy/#ai-connector">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

<h2>Disconnect</h2>
<ol>
<li>In Tuwa: <strong>Profile</strong> › <strong>Legal</strong> › <strong>AI connector</strong>, turn off <strong>Allow the AI connector</strong>. From then on the connector gives your AI nothing more.</li>
<li>In ChatGPT: open <strong>Plugins</strong> and remove or disconnect Tuwa.</li>
</ol>

<ConnectFix locale="en" client="chatgpt" />
</GuidePageLayout>
